  "hints": [
    "sorting gets you O(n log n) - can you do better than sorting?",
    "what if you could check 'have I seen this before?' in O(1) instead of scanning?",
    "what data structure only stores unique values and supports O(1) membership checks?",
    "try a hash set: for each number, check if it's already in the set before adding it"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to check membership before insertion, so the check always fails",
    "using a list instead of a set/hash set for the 'seen' collection, which makes the check O(n) again"
  ],
